<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Cell Biol</journal-id><journal-title>The Journal of Cell Biology</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0021-9525</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1540-8140</issn><publisher><publisher-name>The Rockefeller University Press</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">5678443</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2107516</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>THE TURNOVER OF NUCLEAR DNA-LIKE RNA IN HELA CELLS</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Soeiro</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Vaughan</surname><given-names>M. H.</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Warner</surname><given-names>J. R.</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Darnell</surname><given-names>J. E.</given-names><suffix>Jr.</suffix></name></contrib></contrib-group><aff id="N0x1c0aec0N0x36a8ed8">From the Department of Biochemistry, Albert Einstein College of Medicine, Yeshiva University, New York 10461.</aff><author-notes><fn><p>Dr. Vaughan's present address is the Department of Biochemistry and Nutrition, University of Pittsburgh, Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania 15213</p></fn></author-notes><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><day>1</day><month>10</month><year>1968</year></pub-date><volume>39</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>112</fpage><lpage>118</lpage><history><date date-type="received"><day>17</day><month>4</month><year>1968</year></date><date date-type="rev-recd"><day>27</day><month>5</month><year>1968</year></date></history><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; 1968 by The Rockefeller University Press.</copyright-statement></permissions><abstract><p> The subcellular distribution of various types of RNA in HeLa cells is described. In addition, the relative rate of synthesis of the major classes of nuclear RNA has been determined. From these experiments it can be deduced that the heterogeneous nuclear RNA fraction is rapidly synthesized and degraded within the cell nucleus. </p></abstract></article-meta></front></article>